  <div class="callout warn"><strong>Do not combine the figures.</strong> The 5.5-week value is the current 80% figure displayed on the official visa page. The 15- and 24-working-day values are historical observations from the separate selector and are not presented as current.</div>

  <h2>Why GovWait shows a source mismatch</h2>
  <p>GovWait’s automated New Zealand series follows INZ’s central processing-time selector. That selector included Post Study Work Visa when GovWait recorded the two working-day percentiles on August 23, 2026, but no longer lists the route. GovWait therefore deactivated those current-series entities without deleting their history.</p>
  <p>INZ’s individual Post Study Work Visa page still exists and currently displays a single 80% processing figure of 5.5 weeks. This page identifies the source of each number instead of pretending the route-page figure is a continuation of the older two-percentile selector series.</p>

  <h2>Which figure should a reader use?</h2>
  <p>For a current general planning figure, verify the 5.5-week value directly on the official visa page. Do not use GovWait’s August selector observations as today’s wait, and do not convert either source into a guaranteed decision date for an individual application.</p>
  <p>INZ controls the visa requirements and may change the displayed figure. GovWait cannot see an application, determine eligibility or estimate a personal completion date.</p>

